        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "Experimental Procedure",
          "quote": "The Gleeble 3800 was employed to perform the compression tests at 900 °C, 920 °C, 940 °C, 960 °C, 980 °C and 1050 °C, respectively. The initial stain rate was set as 0.001, 0.01 and 1 s−1. During the hot compression, the specimen was induction heated rapidly to the deforming temperature and kept for 5 mins. Then the compression was performed at constant temperature and the deformation fraction of the tests was about 50%. After compression, the specimen was water quenched to keep the deforming microstructure.",
